dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.brep.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.semio.brep
start body
framing record

# brep wave (following the flow pilot's proven template): REAL binary pack frame, replacing
# the old `serde_json::to_vec`-in-envelope shortcut (`📸️snapshot/🦀️.rs`'s old
# `ArtifactPack::encode_pack_with`). `format u8` (real, fixed) then `schema_len`/`schema_bytes`
# (real, varint-length-prefixed UTF-8 — matches `write_str_lp`'s own wire exactly) are genuinely,
# fully described. Past that, `vertices`/`edges`/`loops`/`faces`/`shells`/`solids` are HOMOGENEOUS
# but variable-length repeated records (each itself holding further variable-length sub-
# collections, and `edges`/`faces` also embed a data-carrying tagged `curve`/`surface` union) — the
# `protocol-array-of-records` gap (`repeat`'s own arms are tag-dispatched, not "repeat N times, N
# from a count field", for an untagged homogeneous record): modeled as one opaque trailing
# `payload` chain, the same honest boundary every P1-P3 pilot's own nested/recursive payload uses.
# The real Rust `encode_brep_snapshot_binary`/`decode_brep_snapshot_binary` stays genuinely, fully
# structured (varint counts, per-field length-prefixes, real `f64` LE coordinates, a real per-
# variant tag byte for `curve`/`surface`) — round-trip tested independently by this facet's own
# tests, only the protocol DESCRIPTION stops at this boundary.
header fixed 1
field format u8

segment schema_len varint
segment schema_bytes Array(u8, Field(schema_len))

chain payload bytes
